BAAI/bge-m3 ONNX auto-embeddings download their external weights and run inference.
––– comment –––
Start Manticore Search with the embeddings module.
––– block: ../base/start-searchd –––
––– comment –––
Creating the table must download both onnx/model.onnx and its model.onnx_data sidecar.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P9306 -e "CREATE TABLE bge_m3 (body TEXT, embedding FLOAT_VECTOR KNN_TYPE='hnsw' HNSW_SIMILARITY='cosine' MODEL_NAME='BAAI/bge-m3' FROM='body')"; echo $?
––– output –––
0
––– comment –––
Insert several Russian documents so auto-embedding exercises ONNX inference without token_type_ids.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P9306 -e "INSERT INTO bge_m3 (id,body) VALUES (1,'хлеб'),(2,'собака'),(3,'кошка')"; echo $?
––– output –––
0
––– comment –––
All documents must be indexed with generated embeddings.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P9306 -N -B -e "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM bge_m3" | grep -oE '[0-9]+'
––– output –––
3
––– comment –––
Text KNN queries must use the same ONNX model and return all indexed documents.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P9306 -N -B -e "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM bge_m3 WHERE knn(embedding,3,'булка')" | grep -oE '[0-9]+'
––– output –––
3